---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout>
    <header class="site-header shell">
        <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Kois Gallery home">
            <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">K</span>
            <span>Kois Gallery</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
            <a href="#workflow">How it works</a>
            <a href="#self-hosted">Self-hosting</a>
            <a href="#status">Status</a>
            <a class="nav-cta" href="https://github.com/kois-studio/gallery">View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="top">
        <section class="hero shell">
            <div class="hero-copy">
                <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Photo delivery, on your terms</p>
                <h1>Beautiful galleries.<br /><em>Your infrastructure.</em></h1>
                <p class="hero-lede">
                    Kois Gallery is a focused, self-hosted photo delivery platform for photographers. Share a polished gallery with clients
                    while keeping control of your photos, storage, and deployment.
                </p>
                <div class="hero-actions">
                    <a class="button button-dark" href="https://github.com/kois-studio/gallery"
                        >Explore the project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                    >
                    <a class="text-link" href="#workflow">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
                </div>
                <p class="hero-note">Public project in active development · license and beta release still pending</p>
            </div>

            <div class="hero-art" aria-label="Abstract preview of a photo gallery" role="img">
                <div class="art-glow"></div>
                <div class="gallery-window">
                    <div class="window-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><small>private gallery</small></div>
                    <div class="window-heading">
                        <div><span class="mini-label">Lino Fajardo</span><strong>A summer in motion</strong></div><span class="window-date"
                            >07 / 26</span
                        >
                    </div>
                    <div class="photo-mosaic">
                        <div class="photo photo-one"></div><div class="photo photo-two"></div><div class="photo photo-three"></div><div
                            class="photo photo-four"
                        >
                        </div><div class="photo photo-five"></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="window-footer"><span>24 photographs</span><span>Private link <i></i></span></div>
                </div>
                <div class="art-stamp"><span>01</span><small>controlled<br />delivery</small></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="principles shell" aria-label="Product principles">
            <div>
                <span class="principle-index">01</span><strong>Your photos</strong><p>
                    Keep the originals and the derivatives under your control.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <span class="principle-index">02</span><strong>Your storage</strong><p>
                    Start with a local filesystem on infrastructure you choose.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <span class="principle-index">03</span><strong>Your infrastructure</strong><p>
                    Run one focused installation instead of renting a platform.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section shell" id="workflow">
            <div class="section-intro">
                <p class="eyebrow">A better handoff</p>
                <h2>From a folder of photographs<br /><em>to a link worth sharing.</em></h2>
                <p>Generic cloud folders move files. Gallery gives the delivery a place, a rhythm, and a point of view.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="steps">
                <article class="step">
                    <span>01</span><div>
                        <h3>Create a gallery</h3><p>Give an event a title, a date, and a simple, shareable identity.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>
                <article class="step">
                    <span>02</span><div>
                        <h3>Upload and process</h3><p>
                            Send a batch and get visible progress while Gallery creates browser-friendly derivatives.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </article>
                <article class="step">
                    <span>03</span><div>
                        <h3>Publish privately</h3><p>Choose a cover, publish a revocable link, and send it wherever your clients are.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>
                <article class="step">
                    <span>04</span><div>
                        <h3>Let people browse</h3><p>Visitors see a responsive gallery and can download an original when they need it.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="self-hosted" id="self-hosted">
            <div class="shell self-hosted-grid">
                <div class="terminal-card" aria-label="Docker Compose installation example">
                    <div class="terminal-top"><span>gallery / installation</span><span class="terminal-status"><i></i> local</span></div>
                    <div class="terminal-body">
                        <p><span class="prompt">$</span> git clone github.com/kois-studio/gallery</p><p>
                            <span class="prompt">$</span> cd gallery
                        </p><p><span class="prompt">$</span> export SETUP_TOKEN=<b>••••••••</b></p><p>
                            <span class="prompt">$</span> docker compose up --build -d
                        </p><p class="terminal-result">Gallery is running at <strong>localhost:3000</strong></p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="self-hosted-copy">
                    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Self-hosted by design</p><h2>
                        Small enough to run.<br /><em>Thoughtful enough to trust.</em>
                    </h2><p>
                        One container. SQLite for metadata. A mounted storage root for photographs. A documented operator boundary that
                        makes it clear what you own and what Gallery does.
                    </p><a class="button button-light" href="https://github.com/kois-studio/gallery/blob/main/deploy/README.md"
                        >Read the setup guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                    >
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section shell capabilities" id="status">
            <div class="section-intro compact">
                <p class="eyebrow">The first release</p><h2>Focused by choice.</h2><p>
                    Gallery is being shaped around the useful path first. The things below are real today; the rest has a place in the
                    roadmap, not in a promise.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="capability-grid">
                <article class="capability capability-current">
                    <span class="capability-mark">✓</span><h3>Ready now</h3><ul>
                        <li>Local administrator setup</li><li>Batch JPEG, PNG, and WebP upload</li><li>
                            Thumbnail and display derivatives
                        </li><li>Revocable private share links</li><li>Responsive browsing and original downloads</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="capability capability-next">
                    <span class="capability-mark">→</span><h3>Earned next</h3><ul>
                        <li>Real event-volume validation</li><li>Backup and restore evidence</li><li>Additional storage adapters</li><li>
                            Selections shaped by real workflow
                        </li><li>Further branding and delivery tools</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="closing shell">
            <p class="eyebrow">Built in the open, carefully</p>
            <h2>A quieter way to<br /><em>deliver the work.</em></h2>
            <p>
                Kois Gallery is a Kois project for photographers who want the presentation of a dedicated service without giving up
                ownership of the system underneath.
            </p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
                <a class="button button-dark" href="https://github.com/kois-studio/gallery"
                    >Follow the build <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                ><a class="text-link" href="https://kois.app">About Kois <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer shell">
        <a class="brand" href="#top"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">K</span><span>Kois Gallery</span></a><p>
            Software &amp; Systems by Kois · 2026
        </p><a href="https://github.com/kois-studio/gallery">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </footer>
</Layout>
